THE ROOT PROBLEM: Content-Type header checks at lines 49 and 128 CANNOT be tested through MockMvc because Spring MVC rejects non-JSON requests BEFORE the controller method runs. @RequestBody requires application/json Content-Type for Jackson to parse it.
THE SOLUTION: Call controller methods DIRECTLY (not through MockMvc) to test Content-Type branches. This bypasses Spring's content negotiation.
