## Key Learnings

### 1. Validation Constraints Affect Testability
- `@NotEmpty` validation prevents testing null values via MockMvc
- Spring MVC validation runs BEFORE controller logic
- Some branches may be unreachable due to framework constraints

### 2. Optional.empty() Testing Pattern
```java
when(orderService.findById(999L)).thenReturn(Optional.empty());
mockMvc.perform(put("/api/orders/999")...)
 .andExpect(status().isNotFound());
```
This pattern is essential for covering `.orElse()` branches.

### 3. StringBuilder.length() Branch Testing
To test `if (sb.length() &gt; 0)` FALSE branches:
- Test each field as the FIRST field in the address
- This ensures `sb.length() == 0` when the condition is checked
- Validates that no separator is added when StringBuilder is empty

### 4. Mocking for Exception Handlers
```java
when(httpServletRequest.getRequestURI()).thenReturn(null);
```
Mocking framework objects allows testing edge cases like null paths.

