## How to Achieve 100% Coverage

If absolute 100% coverage is required, here are three approaches:

### Option 1: Modify Source Code to Accept totalAmount

**Change OrderRequest.java**:
```java
public class OrderRequest {
 private Long userId;
 private Long restaurantId;
 private Object deliveryAddress;

 @NotEmpty(message = "Order items cannot be empty")
 @Valid
 private List&lt;OrderItemRequest&gt; items;

 // ADD THIS FIELD
 private BigDecimal totalAmount;

 // ADD GETTER/SETTER
 public BigDecimal getTotalAmount() { return totalAmount; }
 public void setTotalAmount(BigDecimal totalAmount) { this.totalAmount = totalAmount; }
}
```

**Change OrderController.java**:
```java
@PostMapping
public ResponseEntity&lt;Order&gt; createOrder(@Valid @RequestBody OrderRequest request) {
 Order order = new Order();
 // ... existing code ...

 // ADD THIS LOGIC
 if (request.getTotalAmount() != null) {
 order.setTotalAmount(request.getTotalAmount());
 }

 // Now this condition can be FALSE
 if (order.getTotalAmount() == null &amp;&amp; order.getOrderItems() != null) {
 // Calculate total
 }
}
```

**Test**:
```java
@Test
void createOrder_WithTotalAmountSet_ShouldNotRecalculate() throws Exception {
 OrderRequest request = new OrderRequest();
 request.setUserId(100L);
 request.setRestaurantId(200L);
 request.setDeliveryAddress("123 Main St");
 request.setItems(List.of(new OrderItemRequest(1L, 2, BigDecimal.valueOf(10))));
 request.setTotalAmount(BigDecimal.valueOf(50)); // Pre-set total

 mockMvc.perform(post("/api/orders")
 .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
 .content(objectMapper.writeValueAsString(request)))
 .andExpect(status().isCreated());

 // Now line 53 FALSE branch is covered
}
```

### Option 2: Add JaCoCo Exclusion

**Modify order-service/pom.xml**:
```xml
&lt;plugin&gt;
 &lt;groupId&gt;org.jacoco&lt;/groupId&gt;
 &lt;artifactId&gt;jacoco-maven-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
 &lt;version&gt;0.8.11&lt;/version&gt;
 &lt;configuration&gt;
 &lt;excludes&gt;
 &lt;!-- Exclude unreachable lambda in OrderController --&gt;
 &lt;exclude&gt;**/OrderController.lambda$createOrder$1*&lt;/exclude&gt;
 &lt;/excludes&gt;
 &lt;/configuration&gt;
 &lt;executions&gt;
 &lt;execution&gt;
 &lt;goals&gt;
 &lt;goal&gt;prepare-agent&lt;/goal&gt;
 &lt;/goals&gt;
 &lt;/execution&gt;
 &lt;execution&gt;
 &lt;id&gt;report&lt;/id&gt;
 &lt;phase&gt;test&lt;/phase&gt;
 &lt;goals&gt;
 &lt;goal&gt;report&lt;/goal&gt;
 &lt;/goals&gt;
 &lt;/execution&gt;
 &lt;/executions&gt;
&lt;/plugin&gt;
```

**Result**: JaCoCo will ignore the lambda expression, reporting 100% coverage.

### Option 3: Refactor Total Calculation

**Extract method**:
```java
@PostMapping
public ResponseEntity&lt;Order&gt; createOrder(@Valid @RequestBody OrderRequest request) {
 Order order = new Order();
 // ... existing code ...

 if (order.getTotalAmount() == null &amp;&amp; order.getOrderItems() != null) {
 order.setTotalAmount(calculateOrderTotal(order.getOrderItems()));
 }
}

// NEW METHOD - easier to test
private BigDecimal calculateOrderTotal(List&lt;OrderItem&gt; items) {
 return items.stream()
 .map(i -&gt; i.getPrice().multiply(BigDecimal.valueOf(i.getQuantity())))
 .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);
}
```

**Test the extracted method**:
```java
@Test
void calculateOrderTotal_ShouldSumItemPrices() {
 OrderController controller = new OrderController();

 List&lt;OrderItem&gt; items = List.of(
 new OrderItem(1L, 2, BigDecimal.valueOf(10)),
 new OrderItem(2L, 3, BigDecimal.valueOf(5))
 );

 // Use reflection to call private method
 BigDecimal total = ReflectionTestUtils.invokeMethod(
 controller, "calculateOrderTotal", items
 );

 assertEquals(BigDecimal.valueOf(35), total); // 2*10 + 3*5 = 35
}
```

