## What Was Modified

### Problem Identified

The user reported **4 missed branches** in `OrderController.java`:
1. **Line 37**: `if (request.getItems() != null)` - FALSE path (items=null) NOT TESTED
2. **Line 53**: `if (order.getTotalAmount() == null &amp;&amp; order.getOrderItems() != null)` - FALSE path NOT TESTED
3-4. **Line 53**: Compound AND condition has unreachable branches

### Root Cause Analysis

**Critical Discovery**: The `OrderRequest` DTO has `@NotEmpty` validation on the `items` field:
```java
@NotEmpty(message = "Order items cannot be empty")
@Valid
private List&lt;OrderItemRequest&gt; items;
```

**Impact**: 
- Spring MVC validation runs **BEFORE** controller logic
- Any request with `items=null` is rejected with 400 Bad Request
- Controller code at line 37 is **never reached** via MockMvc
- Cannot test the FALSE path using standard Spring MVC testing

### Solution Implemented

**Strategy**: Call the controller method **DIRECTLY** using `ReflectionTestUtils` to bypass `@Valid` annotation processing.

**Test Method Added**:
```java
@Test
void createOrder_NullItems_ShouldCreateWithoutItems() {
 // Direct controller call bypasses @Valid validation
 OrderController controller = new OrderController();
 ReflectionTestUtils.setField(controller, "orderService", orderService);

 // Create request with ALL required fields EXCEPT items (leave null)
 OrderRequest request = new OrderRequest();
 request.setUserId(100L);
 request.setRestaurantId(200L);
 request.setDeliveryAddress("123 Main St, City, State 12345");
 // DO NOT set items - leave null to cover line 37 FALSE path

 // Mock service to return valid order
 Order savedOrder = new Order();
 savedOrder.setId(1L);
 savedOrder.setUserId(100L);
 savedOrder.setRestaurantId(200L);
 savedOrder.setDeliveryAddress("123 Main St, City, State 12345");
 savedOrder.setStatus(OrderStatus.CREATED);
 savedOrder.setTotalAmount(BigDecimal.ZERO);
 savedOrder.setCreatedAt(LocalDateTime.now());
 savedOrder.setUpdatedAt(LocalDateTime.now());

 when(orderService.createOrderFromEntity(any(Order.class))).thenReturn(savedOrder);

 // Call controller directly
 ResponseEntity&lt;Order&gt; response = controller.createOrder(request);

 // Verify response
 assertEquals(HttpStatus.CREATED, response.getStatusCode());
 assertNotNull(response.getBody());
 assertEquals(1L, response.getBody().getId());

 // Verify service was called
 verify(orderService, times(1)).createOrderFromEntity(any(Order.class));
}
```

**Coverage Achieved**:
- ✅ **Line 37 FALSE path**: `if (request.getItems() != null)` when items is NULL
- ✅ **Line 53 FALSE path**: `order.getOrderItems() == null` (second condition of compound AND)

