## How to Achieve 100% Coverage

If absolute 100% coverage is required, here are three approaches:

### Option 1: Modify Source Code to Accept totalAmount

**Change OrderRequest.java**:
```java
public class OrderRequest {
 private Long userId;
 private Long restaurantId;
 private Object deliveryAddress;

 @NotEmpty(message = "Order items cannot be empty")
 @Valid
 private List&lt;OrderItemRequest&gt; items;

 // ADD THIS FIELD
 private BigDecimal totalAmount;

 // ADD GETTER/SETTER
 public BigDecimal getTotalAmount() { return totalAmount; }
 public void setTotalAmount(BigDecimal totalAmount) { this.totalAmount = totalAmount; }
}
```

**Change OrderController.java**:
```java
@PostMapping
public ResponseEntity&lt;Order&gt; createOrder(@Valid @RequestBody OrderRequest request) {
 Order order = new Order();
 // ... existing code ...

 // ADD THIS LOGIC
 if (request.getTotalAmount() != null) {
 order.setTotalAmount(request.getTotalAmount());
 }

 // Now this condition can be FALSE
 if (order.getTotalAmount() == null &amp;&amp; order.getOrderItems() != null) {
 // Calculate total
 }
}
```

**Test**:
```java
@Test
void createOrder_WithTotalAmountSet_ShouldNotRecalculate() throws Exception {
 OrderRequest request = new OrderRequest();
 request.setUserId(100L);
 request.setRestaurantId(200L);
 request.setDeliveryAddress("123 Main St");
 request.setItems(List.of(new OrderItemRequest(1L, 2, BigDecimal.valueOf(10))));
 request.setTotalAmount(BigDecimal.valueOf(50)); // Pre-set total

 mockMvc.perform(post("/api/orders")
 .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
 .content(objectMapper.writeValueAsString(request)))
 .andExpect(status().isCreated());

 // Now line 53 FALSE branch is covered
}
```

