## JaCoCo Branch Breakdown

### Why 3 Missed Branches Instead of 1?

The compound boolean expression creates multiple branch points:

```java
if (order.getTotalAmount() == null &amp;&amp; order.getOrderItems() != null)
```

**JaCoCo Branch Instrumentation**:

| Branch # | Condition | Left Side | Right Side | Status |
|----------|-----------|-----------|------------|--------|
| 1 | Both TRUE | `totalAmount == null` ✅ | `orderItems != null` ✅ | ✅ **COVERED** |
| 2 | Left TRUE, Right FALSE | `totalAmount == null` ✅ | `orderItems == null` ✅ | ✅ **COVERED** |
| 3 | Left FALSE (short-circuit) | `totalAmount != null` ❌ | N/A | ❌ **UNREACHABLE** |

**Additional Missed Instructions**:
- Lines 56-59: Lambda expression inside the TRUE branch
- JaCoCo reports these as part of the "3 missed branches" count
- The lambda **IS executed** by existing tests, but JaCoCo has instrumentation issues with lambdas

